   $q$Maya's savings grow in a proportional relationship; the graph is a line through the origin that rises 15 dollars every 2 weeks. Leo's savings follow $s = 8w$, where $s$ is dollars and $w$ is weeks. Both start at 0 dollars. After how many weeks will Leo have 10 dollars more than Maya?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-instead-of-divided"},{"text":"$20$","is_correct":true},{"text":"Never, because Maya always saves more","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compared-total-to-rate"},{"text":"$1.25$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-one-rate-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$20$$q$, $q$Maya saves $15 \div 2 = 7.5$ dollars per week and Leo saves 8, so Leo gains $0.5$ dollar each week. To get 10 dollars ahead takes $10 \div 0.5 = 20$ weeks. Saying Maya always saves more compares Maya's 15 dollars for 2 weeks with Leo's 8 dollars for 1 week.$q$, 'draft', null)
