   $q$Which relationship has the same constant of proportionality as $y = 0.6x$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A line through $(0, 0.6)$ and $(1, 1.6)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thinks-y-intercept-is-rate"},{"text":"A table where $x = 10, 25, 40$ gives $y = 6, 15, 24$","is_correct":true},{"text":"A line through the origin and $(9, 15)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-rate"},{"text":"A table where $x = 10, 20, 30$ gives $y = 6, 16, 26$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"additive-pattern"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A table where $x = 10, 25, 40$ gives $y = 6, 15, 24$$q$, $q$In the table with $x = 10, 25, 40$, every ratio is $6 \div 10 = 15 \div 25 = 24 \div 40 = 0.6$. The other table starts at $6 \div 10 = 0.6$, but $16 \div 20 = 0.8$, because it adds 10 each time instead of keeping a constant ratio.$q$, 'draft', null)
