   $q$A bus travels at a constant speed; its graph of miles against hours is a line through the origin and $(2.5, 150)$. A train travels 260 miles in 4 hours at a constant speed. Both leave the same station at the same time going the same direction. How many miles apart are they after 3.5 hours?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$17.5$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-multiply-by-time"},{"text":"$437.5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-rates"},{"text":"$110$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compared-point-values"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$17.5$$q$, $q$The bus goes $150 \div 2.5 = 60$ miles per hour and the train goes $260 \div 4 = 65$ miles per hour, so the gap grows by 5 miles each hour. After 3.5 hours they are $5 \times 3.5 = 17.5$ miles apart. The choice $5$ is the gap after only 1 hour.$q$, 'draft', null)
